{
  "name": "When to re-stain your log home in Colorado",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It's super important to keep an eye on your log home's stain, especially here in Colorado where the elements can be tough. Folks often ask how often they should re-stain, and honestly, it varies a bit. Generally, you'll need to re-stain about every 3 years, but some stains and exposures might let you go 5-7 years. A good rule of thumb is to check if water still beads on the surface. If it soaks in, that's a clear sign you're due for a refresh. Don't wait too long after you notice the water isn't beading anymore! Regular cleaning, at least once a year, helps a lot too, and it's a great time to inspect for any early signs of trouble. Remember, applying a quality stain specifically designed for log homes is key; generic exterior coatings just won't cut it. If you're unsure whether your existing finish can be re-coated or needs stripping, or if you spot any rot, it's a good idea to reach out to a professional. We're happy to help you figure out the best approach for your home.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
